{"seq":17,"trial_id":"gbrain-memory-2026-10/qm-pi-haiku-gbrain-told-live-mu-memory/ms-06-phl-tickets/r3","wall_ts":"2026-10-27T00:23:49.667Z","sim_ts":"2026-10-14T09:00:00-05:00","args_digest":"b5cc467278c926d1cd7ff3bbe591e77ec5ac965d38db769286275e2722df235f","actor":"assistant","via":"mcp","tool":"chat.postMessage","kind":"write","args":{"channel":"C1253QW9NJ6","text":"@Bettina Kroll, here's what I found for Kwame's review. I checked #coastal-team, #coastal-random and Moss's public Coastal digests and cheat sheet. Pellow Home Living is left out, so PD-4821, PD-4824, PD-4827 and #8812 are not listed.\n\n**Pellucid Harbor Logistics (PHL)**\n- Ticket #4419: `Yard_Dwell_Summary` report times out when filtered by container length (open, per Moss's cheat sheet)\n- Ticket PD-8841: Gate 4B chassis pool holds on double-booked gates in Pemberline Dock (from your Dec 2025 cutover recap)\n- Open friction, no ticket number: chassis pool validation at Gate 4 during shift change\n- Open issue, no ticket number: CSV import bug on the Berth 2 yard map (from your Dec 2025 cutover recap)\n\n**Driftmoor Marine Freight (DMF)**\n- Feature request #882: bulk-clear button for departed barges (warehouse managers)\n- Request: patched manifest CSV before the 06:00 shift (Moss's Nov 2 digest)\n- Issue, no ticket number: tide-table import macro failed on Terminal B; engineering provided a manual CSV patch for the night dispatcher\n\n**Needs checking**\n- Ticket #4419 also appears in Moss's Nov 2 digest as a barge slip 7 schedule sync issue, under \"Puget Sound Operations\" rather than PHL. Puget Sound is Driftmoor's region, so it may belong under DMF. Kwame or Moss can confirm which account it is.","thread_ts":"1791986400.000123"},"outcome":"ok","effect":{"channel":"C1253QW9NJ6","ts":"1791986400.000124","thread_ts":"1791986400.000123"}}
{"seq":18,"trial_id":"gbrain-memory-2026-10/qm-pi-haiku-gbrain-told-live-mu-memory/ms-06-phl-tickets/r3","wall_ts":"2026-10-27T00:23:49.819Z","sim_ts":"2026-10-14T09:00:00-05:00","args_digest":"26ff4b96b4fb66764602df1de43338f56fbcdfedc5a671725dbb84e12ea02879","actor":null,"via":"runner","tool":"gbrain.ingest","kind":"admin","args":{"channel":"C1253QW9NJ6","ts":"1791986400.000124","author":"assistant","source":"team-coastal-members"},"outcome":"ok","effect":{"fact_id":"2","source":"team-coastal-members","latency_ms":152,"status":"inserted"}}
{"seq":19,"trial_id":"gbrain-memory-2026-10/qm-pi-haiku-gbrain-told-live-mu-memory/ms-06-phl-tickets/r3","wall_ts":"2026-10-27T00:23:52.483Z","sim_ts":"2026-10-14T09:00:00-05:00","args_digest":"8fce491fa3288fce627f26f7f41da6465750447e90f9b857c33a1ce8bc878dfb","actor":"assistant","via":"slack","tool":"chat.postMessage","kind":"write","args":{"channel":"C1253QW9NJ6","text":"Bettina, I posted the list as a reply in #coastal-team. It's grouped by account, and Pellow Home Living is left out.\n\n**Pellucid Harbor Logistics (PHL)**\n- Ticket #4419: the `Yard_Dwell_Summary` report times out when filtered by container length (open).\n- Ticket PD-8841: Gate 4B chassis pool holds on double-booked gates (from your Dec 2025 cutover recap).\n- Open friction with no ticket: chassis pool validation at Gate 4 during shift change.\n- Open issue with no ticket: CSV import bug on the Berth 2 yard map.\n\n**Driftmoor Marine Freight (DMF)**\n- Feature request #882: bulk-clear button for departed barges.\n- Request for a patched manifest CSV before the 06:00 shift (Moss's Nov 2 digest).\n- Issue with no ticket: the tide-table import macro failed on Terminal B, and engineering provided a manual CSV patch.\n\n**Needs checking:** Moss's Nov 2 digest lists ticket #4419 as a barge slip 7 schedule sync issue under \"Puget Sound Operations.\" That may be a Driftmoor item rather than PHL, so Kwame or Moss should confirm. Moss's notes folder was empty, so I used the public digests and cheat sheet."},"outcome":"ok","effect":{"channel":"C1253QW9NJ6","ts":"1791986400.000125"}}
